      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Although the issue is specifically urologic, scrotal pain and/or enlargement is not an exception at the general practitioner's outpatient clinic. Besides testicular torsion, usually managed in an emergency division setting, there are four frequent diagnoses: testicular tumor, orchi-epididimytis, hydrocele or spermatocele, so as varicocele. The purpose of this article is to provide an update and allow to easily identify serious or frequent scrotal pathologies in primary care medecine."},
